The publish gate. While this file exists the release workflow tags nothing.

yze-yml-wfpolicy is not published yet, and every push while it was unheld minted
a version: v0.1.0 and v0.2.0 both point at trees carrying defects an adversarial
review has since found and repaired — among them a symlinked directory argument
answered with a silent clean pass, no size bound at all, and a run emptied by a
single unreadable file.

Those tags cost nothing today only because the repository is private and
proxy.golang.org has never been asked for this module — the first fetch after it
goes public would cache whichever tree it lands on, permanently, and
sum.golang.org would record its hash forever.

So the hold stays until publication is a decision rather than a side effect of a
push: the leak vet passes over the whole tree and its full history, an
adversarial round returns clean, the stale tags are deleted, and only then is a
single v0.1.0 cut deliberately from a tree somebody chose.

Removing this file IS the act of publishing. Do not remove it to quiet a
workflow.
